the story of Despicable Me 3 was a much  tougher nut to crack for a screenwriters  than the first two films in the  franchise which means that there are a  number of scenes that wound up being  deleted and several concepts that ended  up rejected from the final version of  illuminations latest animated movie  yippee-ki-yay movie lovers it's Jan here  and in this video I'm going to reveal  and explain some of the scenes and ideas  that were cut from the theatrical  release of Despicable Me 3 I've also got  several sets of awesome merchandise from  the movie to give away for a chance to  win make sure you subscribe and turn on  your notifications and answer the  question I'll be asking later in the  video  a quick reminder there are some spoilers  in this video so take care if you  haven't seen the movie yet Despicable Me  3 screenwriters Cinco Paul and Ken Dario  have said they had trouble finding the  right role for Lucy in this movie  indeed in early drafts of the script  Lucy's role was going to be very  different to what we see in the final  movie originally once GRU and his family  arrived in Fredonia Lucy was going to  start fighting crime there actually if  you think about it this storyline would  have fit in rather nicely with how  Lucy's character was first established  in Despicable Me 2 where she was an  undercover agent for the anti-villain  league and obviously enjoyed her job  fighting crime so it makes sense she  would miss that part of her life when  she and gruha fired from the AVL in this  movie and given the way that Lucy used  various gadgets including a tranquilizer  gun and lipstick taser in the second  film I can't help but wonder what new  gadget she would have used in her  crime-fighting Despicable Me 3 if the  filmmakers had gone ahead with that  storyline what we do know though is that  during the movies cheese festival in  Freedonia there was a big scene cut that  would have featured Lucy chasing after a  robber who's stolen an old woman's purse  as you can imagine from the kind of  humour we see in the despicable Me  movies this deleted scene was full of  slapstick moments as well as  cheese-based puns and sight gags for  instance Lucy was going to have to dodge  a whole load of statues made of cheese  and other cheesy stuff along the way as  she raced after the purse-snatcher and  when she finally caught him she was  going to tell him that this is nacho day  in the end though the screenwriters  decided Lucy's vigilante storyline was  too disconnected from the rest of the  movie and they wanted her story to have  more of an emotional payoff this time so  they focused their attention on building  up Lucy's  nation ship with Margo Edith and Agnes  and how she deals with becoming their  stepmom in fact that decision meant that  Lucy's storyline in this film took a  similar path to grooves in the first  Despicable Me movie as both Lucy and GRU  faced challenges becoming apparent to  the girls but ended up becoming close to  them and later saved their lives after  they're kidnapped by the movies villain  despite all that I think I still would  have preferred the more active and  action-packed crime-fighting storyline  for Lucy in this movie although former  child star Balthazar Bratz is very  clearly the new big bad who team GRU has  to defeat and Despicable Me 3 the  filmmakers didn't always have Bratz in  mind to be their movies number one  villain you see one of the first ideas  for the movie was that brat was just a  henchman to another big super villain he  was the main focus of the film however  that original super villain was pretty  humorless and just didn't work for the  movie because as Despicable Me 3  producer Chris Mallard andriy has said  you need to give GRU a worthy adversary  someone who presents a real challenge as  well as someone who is worthy comedic  Lee Grimm is so fun and lively that if  you put a very straight villain against  him that character will just disappear  fortunately when the filmmakers saw the  animators early sketches of beltasar  brats they realized that his character  had a lot more potential than they first  thought and that he was actually the  worthy adversary for GRU that they'd  been looking for  so they upgraded brats role from a mere  sidekick to a 1980s obsessed super  villain out to destroy Hollywood  speaking of Balthasar brats fixation  with all things 1980s of course that  means the movie contains a ton of  pop-culture references to fashion TV  shows movies and music from that decade  but it's not everything the screen ride  has had in mind to show off brats 80's  mania made it into the final cut of the  film  for example Trey Parker who provides the  voice of Balthazar brat and is best  known as co-creator and star of South  Park recorded a bunch of songs for used  in the movie including karma chameleon a  classic song from 1983 by the British  band culture club  however those songs ended up on the  cutting room floor when the scene where  Bratz was going to sing a track from the  1980s was completely dropped from the  movie however we do still get to hear  voice actor Trey Parker sing in the  movie but now it's a new track called  hug me which was written by Pharrell  Williams  by the way I've made a separate  video about all the cool Easter eggs and  movie references in Despicable Me 3 and  there's a link to that in the video  description below and at the end of this  video  long-lost twin brothers grew and drew  our opposites in many ways and their  contrasting personalities influenced the  filmmakers design of drew in fact Drew's  luck in the final film including his  flowing blond hair and white suit versus  Gru's bald head and dark clothes was one  of co-director Eric Yeon's first designs  for drew however before the filmmakers  finally decided on that particular look  for grooves new brother  they tried out a variety of other looks  including having drew wear a big fur  coat over a sweatshirt a design which  emphasized that drew was both very  laid-back and very wealthy thanks to  having inherited his father's enormous  fortune and pig farm in the end though  that look was rejected in favor of their  first design which the filmmakers felt  reflected Drew's personality and a much  simpler and clearer way the clear-cut  differences between the newly reunited  twin brothers are played up during a  family dinner scene which was also the  subject of several cuts this scene were  grew and drew swapped clothes and  hairstyles and generally clown around  pretending to be each other started out  quite a bit longer than the scene we see  in the final film with the brothers  back-and-forth banter initially  stretching out to over three minutes the  scene was actually rather complicated a  Steve Carell who voices grew and drew  had to play each character imitating the  other character in a conversation  between themselves so to make it easier  Carell recorded all grieves lines first  they went back and recorded all Drew's  lines later  there's also another funny moment that  takes place at Drew's mansion in  Freedonia which was cut from the final  movie in the deleted scene grew and drew  are wearing their new spy costumes and  are examining one of Drew's many weapons  when suddenly Lucy walks in on them in  his pretty annoyed as she thinks they're  now both going to be villains no you too  are villains  ah I mean hello speedy  although this scene ended up being  deleted it looks like there's a little  trace of what the filmmakers were going  for with this moment in the final film  just after Lucy sends away Niko's mother  for cursing Margo she walks towards the  window in Drew's mansion and spots GRU  and drew in their spy costumes jetting  off in their speedboat Lucy looks pretty  annoyed like she knows something is  going on and thinks the brothers are up  to no good which likely relates back to  that deleted scene where she discovered  GRU and drew in their lair now what do 